        "description": "Use this tool whenever the user asks to generate, create, draw, visualize,\nor make an image.\n\nThe \"prompt\" input MUST be a detailed image-generation prompt written\nin English.\n\nBefore calling the tool, analyze what the user wants to see and create\na visually precise prompt.\n\nIMPORTANT COMPOSITION RULES:\n\n- If the user asks for a city, country, place, landscape, architecture,\n  historical location, or historical event, focus on the environment,\n  architecture and landscape.\n\n- Do NOT generate a portrait unless the user specifically asks for a portrait.\n\n- Do NOT make a single person the main subject when the request is about\n  a city, country, place or historical environment.\n\n- For cities and locations, prefer wide-angle or panoramic compositions.\n\n- For historical scenes, include:\n  historical period,\n  approximate century,\n  architecture,\n  clothing appropriate to the period,\n  geography,\n  landscape,\n  atmosphere,\n  realistic composition.\n\n- Explicitly include negative composition instructions when appropriate:\n  \"no portrait, no close-up face, no single person as the main subject\".\n\nExample:\n\nUser request:\n\"Show me how Baku looked 1400 years ago\"\n\nPrompt:\n\"Wide panoramic historical reconstruction of an ancient settlement\nin the area of modern Baku, Azerbaijan, approximately 1400 years ago,\naround the 7th century AD. Caspian Sea coastline, ancient stone buildings,\nearly Caucasian architecture, historically inspired settlement,\nlocal people in period-appropriate clothing, dry coastal landscape,\nrealistic archaeological atmosphere, cinematic natural lighting,\nhighly detailed environment.\n\nWide establishing shot. Focus on the settlement, architecture and landscape.\nNo portrait, no close-up face, no single person as the main subject.\"",
